    "issue": "Webhook events never reach your server",
    "fix": "GitHub needs a publicly reachable URL - localhost never works on its own. Use ngrok while testing locally (and update your GitHub App's webhook URL every time ngrok gives you a new one, unless you're on a paid ngrok plan with a fixed subdomain), then your real deployed URL once live."
  },
  {
    "issue": "AI request failed: No AI provider configured",
    "fix": "Add either AI_PROVIDER=gemini plus GEMINI_API_KEY=... (free, from aistudio.google.com/apikey), or AI_PROVIDER=claude plus ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... (from console.anthropic.com/settings/keys) to your .env file, in the same folder as sdt_ai.py."
  },
  {
    "issue": "401 when posting comments back to GitHub",
    "fix": "A GitHub App installation token expires after about an hour and must be refreshed per request - get_installation_token() already does this on every call rather than caching, so a 401 here usually means the App ID or private key itself doesn't match your GitHub App, not an expiry issue."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Review comments land on the wrong line, or get silently dropped",
    "fix": "This is exactly what filter_valid_comments() in reviewer.py exists to catch - if you're seeing dropped-comment messages in your console, that's the guard working as designed: the AI cited a line number outside the diff's actual range. If a comment you'd expect to see is missing with no drop message logged, check that reviewer.py's build_prompt() is sending the full patch, not a truncated version."
  },
  {
    "issue": "The AI flags too many minor style nitpicks",
    "fix": "build_prompt() in reviewer.py already tells the AI to prioritize bugs, security, and performance over style - if it's still noisy, make that instruction even more explicit (e.g. 'do NOT comment on naming, formatting, or import order under any circumstances') and re-test on the same patch."
  },
  {
    "issue": "The bot approves or blocks PRs when you expected comment-only",
    "fix": "Check decide.py's FORCE_COMMENT_ONLY constant is still True - if you already flipped it to False (Build 4's stretch goal) and want the safe default back, set it back to True. There's no scenario in this project where the bot should skip straight to auto-approving without you deliberately choosing that."
  }
